# Plugins

Two tiers, both without CGO: Go subprocess plugins, and Cardigann YAML definitions. Plugins are not `plugin.Open` shared libraries.

- Go plugins speak newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout. Implement `pluginsdk.Plugin` (`Manifest`, `Configure`) plus the capability you provide. Current interfaces: `IndexerPlugin`, `DownloadClientPlugin`, `MetadataPlugin`, `NotificationPlugin`. Add a new capability on the SDK (including a future `MediaModulePlugin`) before the host calls it.
- `ConfigSchema` on the manifest is what the React plugins tab renders. Do not hard-code a settings form per plugin.
- Call `pluginsdk.Serve` from `main`. Plugin code may import `pkg/pluginsdk` and the standard library only — never `internal/`.
- Build with `CGO_ENABLED=0`. Dev binaries go to `bin/plugins` (`make build-plugins`). Runtime scans `REPLACEARR_PLUGIN_DIR` (`/config/plugins` in Docker).
- Cardigann YAML is data, loaded by `internal/indexers/cardigann` from `REPLACEARR_DEFINITIONS_DIR` (dev: `.tmp/ProwlarrIndexers/definitions/`). It is not a Go plugin.

```go
// BAD: plugin importing the server
import "github.com/replacearr/replacearr/internal/domain"

// GOOD: SDK-only plugin
func main() {
    pluginsdk.Serve(&CustomIndexer{})
}
```
